# Intent: Talking over the robot, wired (off by default, CONFIG_MAIPAI_TALK_OVER_AEC, needs CONFIG_MAIPAI_TALK_OVER): the audio front end gets microphone 1 and the speaker loopback (TDM slot 1) as its two channels (input format MR, echo canceller on, in PSRAM-heavy mode) and cancels the echo on the unit ahead of the wake word. While the unit speaks, the second wake hit within one second interrupts it (maipai_barge_core.h, host test); a sentence the host marks no_barge (with duration_ms) is never interrupted; late frames of an interrupted reply are dropped until the next tts start. A bench build prints one trace line a second, "AEC mic=<rms> ref=<rms> out=<rms>". Off: the image is byte-identical in static RAM and code to the build without it.
# Placement: unit
# Upstream: firmware/xiaozhi-esp32/main/audio/engines/afe_audio_engine.cc and main/application.cc (nested tree, MIT); firmware/main (ours)
# Check after a flash: on an image built with the aec overlay the trace shows out well below mic while a reply plays; two wake words within a second stop the reply and start a new turn; one wake word does nothing while speaking; scripts/fw-voice-bench.py --watch aec|barge|soak gives the verdicts.
# Kconfig: CONFIG_MAIPAI_TALK_OVER_AEC (default n)

diff --git a/firmware/main/Kconfig.projbuild b/firmware/main/Kconfig.projbuild
--- a/firmware/main/Kconfig.projbuild
+++ b/firmware/main/Kconfig.projbuild
@@ -331,6 +331,15 @@ config MAIPAI_TALK_OVER
