         tool measures a tone on both channels. Off: the build is the one without it (MIC1 and MIC2), no code and no memory.
 
+config MAIPAI_TALK_OVER_AEC
+    bool "Talk over the robot: echo canceller on the unit and wake-word interruption while it speaks"
+    depends on MAIPAI_TALK_OVER
+    default n
+    help
+        Patch SF29 (docs/plan, design-talk-over): the audio front end gets microphone 1 and the speaker loopback (TDM slot 1) as its two channels and
+        cancels the echo on the unit, ahead of the wake word. While the unit speaks, the second wake hit within one second interrupts it
+        (maipai_barge_core.h). Off: the build is the one without it, no code and no memory.
+
 config MAIPAI_MIC3_GAIN_DB
     int "Gain of the MIC3 channel in dB (0 to 37)"
     depends on MAIPAI_TALK_OVER
